<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Montenegro</h1><p class="st-meta">1910 CE – 1918 CE · capital Cetinje</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Montenegro's brief kingdom under Nikola I, which fought in the Balkan Wars and the First World War before being merged into Yugoslavia.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>On the fiftieth anniversary of his reign, on 28 August 1910, Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nikola-i-of-montenegro">Nikola I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-montenegro">Principality of Montenegro</a> proclaimed himself king, with the agreement of the Great Powers. The new kingdom kept its capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cetinje">Cetinje</a> and its constitution of 1905.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Nikola continued to rule as a patriarchal monarch, clashing with opponents who favoured union with <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a>. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-balkan-war">First Balkan War</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/montenegro">Montenegro</a> besieged and took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shkoder">Scutari</a> in 1913, but the powers forced it to hand the town to the new <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/albania">Albania</a>; it did gain much of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sandzak">Sandžak</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/metohija">Metohija</a>, including Peć and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gjakova">Đakovica</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p><a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/montenegro">Montenegro</a> joined <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbia">Serbia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a> but was occupied by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austria-Hungary</a> in January 1916, and Nikola went into exile. In November 1918 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/podgorica-assembly">Podgorica Assembly</a> deposed him and voted for union with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a>, provoking the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christmas-uprising">Christmas Uprising</a> of 1919. Montenegro became part of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/kingdom-of-yugoslavia">Kingdom of Yugoslavia</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-montenegro.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Montenegro" width="320" height="213"><figcaption>Image: w:Kingdom of Montenegro (Vector graphics image by B1mbo) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Montenegro_(1905%E2%80%931918).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1910 CE – 1918 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cetinje</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Nikola I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Serbian Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Serbian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/montenegro">Montenegro</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/kosovo">Kosovo</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kraljevina Crna Gora</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1914&amp;focus=kingdom-of-montenegro" aria-label="Kingdom of Montenegro on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5139 670 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of Montenegro lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5459 926L5459 926M5459 926L5380 747M5459 926L5488 850"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5459 926h0M5380 747h0M5488 850h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5459 926h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5459 926h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cetinje. <a href="/atlas?year=1914&amp;focus=kingdom-of-montenegro">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
